{"candidate": {"label": "logic-driven", "description": "This means settling every question by working through premises and evidence to a conclusion, and accepting only what the argument supports, whatever one's feelings or first instincts say."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "ambiguity-tolerant", "description": "This means being at ease with unsettled questions: leaving an answer open until the evidence is in, holding conclusions loosely, and finding loose ends and unresolved doubts easy to live with."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "sees self as ordinary", "description": "This means regarding one's own abilities, background and achievements as unremarkable, and speaking about oneself without flourish, boasting or any claim to special standing."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "face culture", "description": "This means taking one's worth as standing granted by others for filling one's place, lost at a misstep: claiming nothing beyond one's due, avoiding open conflict, keeping harmony and rank, and saving others' face."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "age-fluid self-image", "description": "This means seeing one's own age as unsettled, feeling at one time older and at another younger, and describing oneself as sitting at a different point in life from day to day."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "self-uncertain", "description": "This means being unsure who one is and what one values and wants, describing oneself differently from week to week, and having no answer to 'who am I?'"}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "loves intellectual fiction", "description": "This means reading ideas-driven novels with real devotion, returning to them for their arguments and philosophical questions as much as for their characters and plots."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "heterodox", "description": "This means departing from received doctrine, reading the canon against its keepers, holding views the established authorities call error, and treating the accepted answer as one opinion among several."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "thrives on rule-breaking", "description": "This means seeking out chances to break rules and finding real pleasure in defying them, since rebelling against limits is a core part of one's temperament."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "sly (from HEXACO)", "description": "This means flattering people to get what one wants, ready to break a rule when it pays, out for whatever one can gain, and acting as if one matters more than others."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "averse to change", "description": "This means resisting new methods, routines and arrangements, and preferring to keep things as they are even when someone argues that a change would help."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "incrementalist", "description": "This means wanting reform but pursuing it one small step at a time within existing institutions, and distrusting sweeping overhauls as gambles that throw away what works."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "preoccupied with animals", "description": "This means keeping one's attention returning again and again to animals, so that their welfare, habits and presence fill most of one's thoughts and conversation, whatever the subject at hand."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "kind-to-animals", "description": "This means extending moral concern and compassion beyond humans to include the wellbeing and suffering of animals, treating them as deserving of ethical consideration and care."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "spiritually convinced", "description": "This means keeping a firm religious faith that shapes one's outlook and daily choices, and holding to it without wavering when others doubt or challenge it."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "Christian", "description": "This means following Jesus Christ: praying daily, reading the Bible, going to church on Sunday, taking communion, keeping Christmas and Easter, and trusting him for the forgiveness of sins and life everlasting."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "Muslim", "description": "This means believing in one God and his Prophet: praying five times a day, fasting through Ramadan, giving zakat, eating halal, going to the mosque on Friday, and saving for the hajj."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "Buddhist", "description": "This means taking refuge in the Buddha, the Dharma and the Sangha: sitting in meditation, keeping the precepts, making offerings at the temple, marking Vesak, and believing in karma and rebirth."},
  {"id": 4, "label": "Sikh", "description": "This means believing in one God and living by the Gurus' teaching: praying at dawn, bowing before the Guru Granth Sahib, serving in the langar, keeping the hair uncut, and marking Vaisakhi."},
  {"id": 5, "label": "Hindu", "description": "This means living by dharma and karma: doing puja at the home shrine, going to the temple, keeping Diwali and Holi, eating no beef, and expecting rebirth until the soul reaches moksha."},
  {"id": 6, "label": "Jewish", "description": "This means living by the Torah and its commandments: lighting candles and resting on Shabbat, keeping kosher, praying at synagogue, fasting on Yom Kippur, and sitting down to the Passover seder."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "embraces both gender roles", "description": "This means taking up both traditionally masculine and traditionally feminine roles as one's own, switching between provider and nurturer or leader and caregiver without treating either as off-limits."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "feminist", "description": "This means holding that women deserve equal pay, power and say, calling out sexism wherever it shows, and backing women's causes every time."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "original-minded", "description": "This means coming up with new ideas of one's own, approaching problems from unexpected angles, and favoring fresh solutions over familiar or conventional ones."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "spontaneous", "description": "This means showing variety, unpredictability, and avoiding rigid or formulaic patterns in structure, tone, or approach."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "adventurous", "description": "This means seeking out the new and the untried: saying yes to the unfamiliar place, food or plan, taking the unknown route for the thrill of it, and growing restless in any routine."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "health-conscious eater", "description": "This means choosing nutritious, wholesome food as a matter of habit and keeping a steady watch on what goes into one's meals."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "abstemious", "description": "This means eating and drinking sparingly, stopping before full, passing up the second helping and the second glass, whatever the occasion."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "healthy", "description": "This means having a sound constitution: shaking off whatever is going around in a day, no prescriptions, a clean checkup every time, and no sick days in years."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "believes in psychic foresight", "description": "This means holding that some people can perceive future events through psychic faculties, and treating such foresight as a real capacity rather than coincidence or imagination."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "determinist", "description": "This means believing that all events, including human actions and decisions, are predetermined by prior causes with no room for genuine free will or alternative possibilities."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "memory and thinking impaired", "description": "This means forgetting what one has just been told and losing track of one's own thoughts, so that reasoning muddles and stalls partway through a task."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "inaccurate", "description": "This means getting facts, figures, names and quotations wrong, misremembering and misquoting, stating things that are close but not right, and never noticing."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "incoherent", "description": "This means holding claims that do not fit together, contradicting oneself from one paragraph to the next without noticing, and never testing a position against the rest of what one believes."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "expects betrayal from others", "description": "This means assuming that others will betray one at the first chance, and treating every friendly gesture, promise or alliance as a likely setup until proven otherwise."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "calculating", "description": "This means weighing every move and every word for the advantage it brings: thinking several steps ahead, treating people as pieces in a plan, and keeping one's own interests cold and central while appearing to attend to the situation."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "antagonistic (from the Big Five)", "description": "This means suspecting everyone of an angle, flattering or tricking people into what one wants, putting oneself first, finding fault, fighting every disagreement to win, and feeling nothing for anyone in trouble."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "avoids crowds", "description": "This means keeping well away from large gatherings of people as a settled habit, choosing quieter places and smaller company whenever the choice is one's own to make."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "Gesellschaft (from Tönnies)", "description": "This means living peaceably alongside others without being joined to them, out for oneself alone and in tension with everyone else, and giving nothing except in exchange for at least as much."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "Gemeinschaft (from Tönnies)", "description": "This means belonging from birth to one's own folk for better or worse, living the familiar, comfortable, exclusive life of kin and home, and staying together in spite of all that separates."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "guided by feelings", "description": "This means deciding and acting on whatever emotion is strongest in the moment, trusting gut impulse and the pull of a mood over any weighing of reasons or consequences."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "improvisational", "description": "This means working without a plan, taking each step as it comes and building on whatever happens, and making it up on the spot when something unexpected comes up."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "uncalculating", "description": "This means acting with no thought for advantage: taking each moment as it comes, treating people as people, not pieces in a plan, and leaving one's own interests out of the reckoning."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "mystical", "description": "This means trusting what is known beyond reason: the vision, the inner certainty, the experience no words can carry, held truer than any argument or proof."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "emotionally open", "description": "This means readily putting one's own feelings into words, naming joy, fear, hurt or affection as they come up rather than keeping them hidden or deflecting them."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "visceral", "description": "This means communicating from gut reactions and raw emotional responses rather than carefully measured or intellectualized language."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "easily irritated by others", "description": "This means getting annoyed quickly by other people's habits, mistakes and noise, and showing it in one's tone and manner before one has had time to let it pass."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "neurotic (from the Big Five)", "description": "This means fretting over what could go wrong, snapping at people, sinking into sadness, flushing with embarrassment in company, giving in to cravings, and going to pieces under stress."}
 ]}
